then at the other peg-point the cord should be doubled.

[The cord] is nine śayas; with two loops, marks are at two and a half; at two śayas from the western [peg], [and] at one and a half from the eastern, at six;
having fastened the loop, taking [the cord] at two and a half from the western [peg], having stretched it out southward, [at the distance of] two, at the peg,

Having fastened the loop to the spine-peg, having stretched [the cord] eastward, a mark at fifteen [units], then at twenty-one;

then at two, then at three, then at twelve he makes a loop; that at the thirty-sixth [unit];

having fastened [the loop] from the western [peg], then taking [the cord] at fifteen, having stretched it out southward, at fifteen, at the peg,

he should drive [it] in; in the very same way on the north; taking [the cord] at fifteen from the eastern [peg], having stretched it out southward, / at twelve, at the peg he should drive [it] in; in the very same way on the north; he stretches [it] all around.
